<Track #fix-provider-switch-admission-and-recovery apiVersion="codument.tech/v1alpha1" version="1" { status = "completed" goal = "Make successful provider calls always commit protocol-neutral request admission evidence and make provider switches atomically recoverable across snapshots." description = "Repair the 20260831145910 session incident: Codex Responses completed transport but failed post-response admission observation, then provider state split across snapshot authorities and switching back to DeepSeek could not continue." question_mode = "decision-tree" question_severity = "auto" commit_mode = "manual" created_at = "2026-08-31T16:13:42.625Z" updated_at = "2026-08-31T19:10:26.561Z" modeling_base_commit = "7ae52ab3c6d87e4dafedec9225bea50844c54b14" engineering_base_commit = "7ae52ab3c6d87e4dafedec9225bea50844c54b14" } (
  <Ports { scope = "track" } [
    <MaterialBundle #behavior_deltas { role = "input" name = "behavior-deltas" domain = "behavior" path = "vfs://./behavior_deltas/" }>
  ]>
  <TaskSpace #space_fix-provider-switch-admission-and-recovery { name = "fix-provider-switch-admission-and-recovery" version = "1" } (
    <SubNodes [
      <TaskGroup #P1 { name = "Incident-shaped RED and authority audit" status = "DONE" priority = "P0" order = 0 } (
        <Description ?01M1CA8J1H0MDK3433E6BBE20P>
        Reproduce the Codex post-response admission failure and the divergent provider snapshot/transition heads without mutating the original session.
        </?01M1CA8J1H0MDK3433E6BBE20P>
        <Gate [
          <Criterion { checked = true } ?01M1CA8J1H0MDK3433E6BBE20Q>
          A deterministic test proves any successful transport has a value-safe request digest independent of DeepSeek cache instrumentation.
          </?01M1CA8J1H0MDK3433E6BBE20Q>
          <Criterion { checked = true } ?01M1CA8J1H0MDK3433E6BBE20R>
          A recovery fixture proves provider receipt/head divergence and swallowed checkpoint errors.
          </?01M1CA8J1H0MDK3433E6BBE20R>
        ]>
        <SubNodes [
          <Task #P1-T1 { name = "Capture provider admission and switch RED" status = "DONE" priority = "P0" order = 0 } (
            <Description ?01M1CA8J1H0MDK3433E6BBE20S>
            Add focused tests from session 20260831145910 for Codex Responses success followed by provider_request_admission_observation_required, and for switch/checkpoint divergence.
            </?01M1CA8J1H0MDK3433E6BBE20S>
            <Acceptance [
              <Criterion #P1-T1-AC1 { checked = true } ?01M1CA8J1H0MDK3433E6BBE20T>
              The Codex case fails at the post-response observation boundary before the fix.
              </?01M1CA8J1H0MDK3433E6BBE20T>
              <Criterion #P1-T1-AC2 { checked = true } ?01M1CA8J1H0MDK3433E6BBE20V>
              The switch case detects a session.index provider epoch newer than provider-context transition head.
              </?01M1CA8J1H0MDK3433E6BBE20V>
              <Criterion #P1-T1-AC3 { checked = true } ?01M1CA8J1H0MDK3433E6BBE20W>
              The original session directory is read-only evidence and remains byte/mtime unchanged.
              </?01M1CA8J1H0MDK3433E6BBE20W>
            ]>
          )>
        ]>
      )>
      <TaskGroup #P2 { name = "Protocol-neutral admission and atomic provider transition" status = "DONE" priority = "P0" order = 1 } (
        <Description ?01M1CA8J1H0MDK3433E6BBE20X>
        Decouple request admission evidence from DeepSeek cache observation and make model control, adapter refresh, provider epoch transition and snapshot commit one recoverable ordering.
        </?01M1CA8J1H0MDK3433E6BBE20X>
        <Gate [
          <Criterion { checked = true } ?01M1CA8J1H0MDK3433E6BBE20Y>
          Every admitted provider request has a digest even when no provider-specific cache observer exists.
          </?01M1CA8J1H0MDK3433E6BBE20Y>
          <Criterion { checked = true } ?01M1CA8J1H0MDK3433E6BBE20Z>
          A committed snapshot cannot expose a new provider receipt with a stale transition head.
          </?01M1CA8J1H0MDK3433E6BBE20Z>
        ]>
        <SubNodes [
          <Task #P2-T1 { name = "Implement universal final-wire request observation" status = "DONE" priority = "P0" order = 0 } (
            <Description ?01M1CA8J1H0MDK3433E6BBE210>
            Produce the safe request digest at common transport admission; provider-specific observers may enrich cache/cost facts but are not required for validity.
            </?01M1CA8J1H0MDK3433E6BBE210>
            <Acceptance [
              <Criterion #P2-T1-AC1 { checked = true } ?01M1CA8J1H0MDK3433E6BBE211>
              OpenAI Responses, OpenAI Chat and DeepSeek Chat all satisfy the common admission evidence contract.
              </?01M1CA8J1H0MDK3433E6BBE211>
              <Criterion #P2-T1-AC2 { checked = true } ?01M1CA8J1H0MDK3433E6BBE212>
              Evidence contains no prompt, tool argument/result or credential values.
              </?01M1CA8J1H0MDK3433E6BBE212>
            ]>
          )>
          <Task #P2-T2 { name = "Implement atomic provider switch and checkpoint failure semantics" status = "DONE" priority = "P0" order = 1 } (
            <Description ?01M1CA8J1H0MDK3433E6BBE213>
            Resolve target adapter/profile before epoch activation, commit transition receipt/head consistently, and surface snapshot failure instead of swallowing it.
            </?01M1CA8J1H0MDK3433E6BBE213>
            <Acceptance [
              <Criterion #P2-T2-AC1 { checked = true } ?01M1CA8J1H0MDK3433E6BBE214>
              Explicit model control refreshes the target adapter before deriving the target protocol profile.
              </?01M1CA8J1H0MDK3433E6BBE214>
              <Criterion #P2-T2-AC2 { checked = true } ?01M1CA8J1H0MDK3433E6BBE215>
              Snapshot and transition head either commit together or leave the last known-good state recoverable.
              </?01M1CA8J1H0MDK3433E6BBE215>
              <Criterion #P2-T2-AC3 { checked = true } ?01M1CA8J1H0MDK3433E6BBE216>
              A checkpoint write failure becomes typed visible evidence and never presents a false idle/stuck state.
              </?01M1CA8J1H0MDK3433E6BBE216>
            ]>
          )>
        ]>
      )>
      <TaskGroup #P3 { name = "Recovery regression and copied-session verification" status = "DONE" priority = "P0" order = 2 } (
        <Description ?01M1CA8J1H0MDK3433E6BBE217>
        Verify failed Codex turns and provider switches can resume with either Codex or DeepSeek from deterministic fixtures and a named copy of the incident session.
        </?01M1CA8J1H0MDK3433E6BBE217>
        <Gate [
          <Criterion { checked = true } ?01M1CA8J1H0MDK3433E6BBE218>
          The copied session can continue after selecting either protocol without local admission/profile errors.
          </?01M1CA8J1H0MDK3433E6BBE218>
          <Criterion { checked = true } ?01M1CA8J1H0MDK3433E6BBE219>
          Focused suites, terminal build, strict Codument validation and diff checks pass.
          </?01M1CA8J1H0MDK3433E6BBE219>
        ]>
        <SubNodes [
          <Task #P3-T1 { name = "Verify provider switch recovery matrix" status = "DONE" priority = "P0" order = 0 } (
            <Description ?01M1CA8J1H0MDK3433E6BBE21A>
            Run Codex→retry, Codex→DeepSeek and DeepSeek→Codex recovery cases, verify authority heads, no duplicate tool effects and original-session immutability.
            </?01M1CA8J1H0MDK3433E6BBE21A>
            <Acceptance [
              <Criterion #P3-T1-AC1 { checked = true } ?01M1CA8J1H0MDK3433E6BBE21B>
              A failed provider turn does not permanently seal the main fiber.
              </?01M1CA8J1H0MDK3433E6BBE21B>
              <Criterion #P3-T1-AC2 { checked = true } ?01M1CA8J1H0MDK3433E6BBE21C>
              Fresh recovery chooses the last committed provider epoch and protocol profile.
              </?01M1CA8J1H0MDK3433E6BBE21C>
              <Criterion #P3-T1-AC3 { checked = true } ?01M1CA8J1H0MDK3433E6BBE21D>
              No duplicate provider/tool effect or canonical history rewrite occurs.
              </?01M1CA8J1H0MDK3433E6BBE21D>
            ]>
          )>
        ]>
      )>
      <TaskGroup #P4 { name = "Interactive actor-target recovery" status = "DONE" priority = "P0" order = 3 } (
        <Description ?01M1CZP4000000000000000001>
        Repair the actual TUI Primary-target submission path so a user message sent through actor.send revives and drives a recovered failed fiber through the same interactive-turn lifecycle instead of returning an idle projection.
        </?01M1CZP4000000000000000001>
        <Gate [
          <Criterion { checked = true } ?01M1CZP4000000000000000002>
          A copied failed session continues through the TUI actor-target API without requiring headless --auto-resume.
          </?01M1CZP4000000000000000002>
          <Criterion { checked = true } ?01M1CZP4000000000000000003>
          User input, provider execution, error projection and persistence form one observable turn; the UI cannot silently retain an input that never reached durable runtime state.
          </?01M1CZP4000000000000000003>
        ]>
        <SubNodes [
          <Task #P4-T1 { name = "Drive recovered actor-target turns to an observable terminal boundary" status = "DONE" priority = "P0" order = 0 } (
            <Description ?01M1CZP4000000000000000004>
            Add an incident-shaped TUI actor.send regression, reuse the runtime coordinator for targeted interactive execution, project failures visibly, and verify the real copied session through the actor API.
            </?01M1CZP4000000000000000004>
            <Acceptance [
              <Criterion #P4-T1-AC1 { checked = true } ?01M1CZP4000000000000000005>
              Sending human input to Primary after recovering a failed fiber SHALL revive that fiber and dispatch a provider turn through the interactive coordinator.
              </?01M1CZP4000000000000000005>
              <Criterion #P4-T1-AC2 { checked = true } ?01M1CZP4000000000000000006>
              The actor-target call SHALL return a refreshed projection only after a settled or human-blocked boundary, and SHALL reject with a visible error on activation, provider, timeout or checkpoint failure.
              </?01M1CZP4000000000000000006>
              <Criterion #P4-T1-AC3 { checked = true } ?01M1CZP4000000000000000007>
              A real copy of session 20260831145910 SHALL continue with DeepSeek and Codex through the same actor-target API, with consistent provider receipt/head and no duplicate tool effect.
              </?01M1CZP4000000000000000007>
            ]>
          )>
        ]>
      )>
      <TaskGroup #P5 { name = "Bounded restored-session runtime initialization" status = "DONE" priority = "P0" order = 4 } (
        <Description ?01M1D0VFS00000000000000001>
        Repair the post-overlay regression where restoring a real session recursively imports runtime-owned home state into Effective Eidolon VFS before MCP startup, exhausting CPU and memory while the TUI misleadingly reports MCP initialization.
        </?01M1D0VFS00000000000000001>
        <Gate [
          <Criterion { checked = true } ?01M1D0VFS00000000000000002>
          Configuration/resource overlays have an explicit root authority boundary and never ingest session/project runtime state.
          </?01M1D0VFS00000000000000002>
          <Criterion { checked = true } ?01M1D0VFS00000000000000003>
          The copied incident session reaches an interactive TUI boundary through eidolon --yolo within bounded time and memory, with and without MCP.
          </?01M1D0VFS00000000000000003>
        ]>
        <SubNodes [
          <Task #P5-T1 { name = "Fence runtime state from Effective VFS startup" status = "DONE" priority = "P0" order = 0 } (
            <Description ?01M1D0VFS00000000000000004>
            Add the incident-shaped RED, define the physical overlay root classification, exclude runtime-owned projects and sessions before traversal, preserve managed configuration/resources, and verify the exact installed TUI restore path.
            </?01M1D0VFS00000000000000004>
            <Acceptance [
              <Criterion #P5-T1-AC1 { checked = true } ?01M1D0VFS00000000000000005>
              A physical overlay containing large projects and sessions trees SHALL omit those roots without traversing or reading their descendants while retaining root configuration and resources.
              </?01M1D0VFS00000000000000005>
              <Criterion #P5-T1-AC2 { checked = true } ?01M1D0VFS00000000000000006>
              Runtime initialization SHALL expose a generic local-runtime preparation state before any actual MCP phase, so a pre-MCP failure is not diagnosed as an MCP hang.
              </?01M1D0VFS00000000000000006>
              <Criterion #P5-T1-AC3 { checked = true } ?01M1D0VFS00000000000000007>
              A fresh copy of session 20260831145910 restored via eidolon --yolo SHALL become interactive within the bounded smoke-test budget without CPU/RSS amplification from home project history; --no-mcp SHALL satisfy the same pre-MCP bound.
              </?01M1D0VFS00000000000000007>
            ]>
          )>
        ]>
      )>
    ]>
